    <briefdescription>
<para>Represents a framebuffer resize event. </para>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para>This class is used to represent a framebuffer resize event, which occurs when the size of the framebuffer changes. It contains two parameters - width and height that specify the new dimensions of the framebuffer. </para>
    </detaileddescription>
